@FixTrack.Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5072
@userA = user-a-token
@userB = user-b-token
@admin = admin-token
# The first POST after restart creates case-105. For later runs, copy the ID from Location.
@createdCaseId = case-105

# Each title shows the expected status. Restart the API to reset the in-memory data.

### View the anonymous greeting — 200 HTML
GET {{FixTrack.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/greeting

### List user A’s cases — 200
GET {{FixTrack.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cases
Authorization: Bearer {{userA}}

### List user B’s cases — 200
GET {{FixTrack.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cases
Authorization: Bearer {{userB}}

### List all cases as admin — 200
GET {{FixTrack.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cases
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### Page through all cases as admin — 200
GET {{FixTrack.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cases?page=1&perPage=2
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### Read user A’s own case — 200
GET {{FixTrack.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cases/case-101
Authorization: Bearer {{userA}}

### Read user B’s case as user A — 404
GET {{FixTrack.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cases/case-103
Authorization: Bearer {{userA}}

### Read a nonexistent case — 404
GET {{FixTrack.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cases/case-999
Authorization: Bearer {{userA}}

### Create a case as user A — 201, with the new case URL in Location
POST {{FixTrack.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cases
Authorization: Bearer {{userA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Alex Morgan",
  "device": "Laptop",
  "issueDescription": "The charging port stops working intermittently.",
  "caseType": "Repair"
}

### Replace the newly created case — 200
PUT {{FixTrack.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cases/{{createdCaseId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Alex Morgan",
  "device": "Laptop",
  "issueDescription": "The charging port stops working intermittently.",
  "caseType": "Repair",
  "status": "InProgress"
}

### Replace user B’s case as user A — 404
PUT {{FixTrack.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cases/case-103
Authorization: Bearer {{userA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Alex Morgan",
  "device": "Laptop",
  "issueDescription": "The charging port stops working intermittently.",
  "caseType": "Repair",
  "status": "InProgress"
}

### Delete the newly created case — 200, with data set to null
DELETE {{FixTrack.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cases/{{createdCaseId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userA}}

### Delete user B’s case as user A — 404
DELETE {{FixTrack.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cases/case-103
Authorization: Bearer {{userA}}

### List cases without a token — 401
GET {{FixTrack.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cases

### List cases with an invalid token — 401
GET {{FixTrack.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cases
Authorization: Bearer nope

### Create with missing required fields — 400
POST {{FixTrack.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cases
Authorization: Bearer {{userA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Create with a one-character customer name — 400
POST {{FixTrack.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cases
Authorization: Bearer {{userA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "A",
  "device": "Laptop",
  "issueDescription": "The charging port stops working intermittently.",
  "caseType": "Repair"
}

### Create with a server-managed ownerId — 400
POST {{FixTrack.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cases
Authorization: Bearer {{userA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Alex Morgan",
  "device": "Laptop",
  "issueDescription": "The charging port stops working intermittently.",
  "caseType": "Repair",
  "ownerId": "user-b"
}

### List with an invalid page size — 400
GET {{FixTrack.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cases?perPage=0
Authorization: Bearer {{userA}}

### Use an unsupported method — 405
PATCH {{FixTrack.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cases/case-101
Authorization: Bearer {{userA}}

### Create with a plain-text body — 415
POST {{FixTrack.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cases
Authorization: Bearer {{userA}}
Content-Type: text/plain

Laptop needs repair.
